<title>USA: Walter Q3 fully diluted shr loss narrows.</title>
<headline>Walter Q3 fully diluted shr loss narrows.</headline>
<dateline>TAMPA, Florida 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997			1996</p>
<p> Shr loss	  $0.04	     loss $2.42</p>
<p> Net loss	  2,200	     loss 123,600</p>
<p> Revs		340,400		  329,100</p>
<p> Avg shrs	  51,142		   50,988</p>
<p>	  9   MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr profit	$0.28	     loss $2.44</p>
<p> Net profit	15,500	    loss 124,400</p>
<p> Revs		1,108,000		1,087,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs	  54,973		   50,988</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Full company name is Walter Industries Inc.</p>
<p>1997 fiscal third quarter and nine months ended February 28.</p>
<p>1997 Q3 had a $6.2 million pre-tax or $4.0 million post-tax charge for a voluntary early retirement program completed in February at the company's coal mining subsidiary.</p>
<p>Prior year net included a $143.3 million pre-tax, or $101.1 million post-tax, non-recurring charge related to the adoption of an accounting standard.</p>
<p>Prior year Q3 net also included extraordinary $5.4 million or $0.10 a share after-tax charge for debt refinancing costs.</p>
</text>
